## Risk & validation
<correctness/blast radius · which test/model/metric confirms it · what to measure>
```

**Method (use multi-agents — fan out, one per category)**
1. From `agendas_research.md`, pick the 5-6 categories with the sharpest patterns
   and widest reach (candidates: `reduce-precision` spread; `fuse`/fusion-pass;
   `reuse`/prefix-caching; `overlap`/compute-comm; shared-abstraction refactor;
   port-the-proven-win to ROCm/TPU/CPU). Close categories may be merged.
2. Launch one agent per category **in parallel** (independent search spaces). Give
   each the pattern recipe, the source root, and the dedupe rule. Each agent:
   greps the source for the pattern's signature, reads the candidate functions,
   confirms it is not an existing PR, writes `localization.md` + `solution.md`.
3. Draft every candidate with the full `solution.md` including its `## Critique`.
4. **Critique + filter pass.** Re-read each proposal's `## Critique` and cut the
   weak ones: too small a fraction of runtime, already done implicitly by the
   backend, correctness landmine, speculative gain with no precedent. Filtering a
   whole category is allowed if none of its proposals survive. Keep the strongest
   (5-8 typical, 10 max per surviving category). Record what you cut and why — it
   feeds `experiments/report.md`.
5. Write each surviving category `README.md` (pattern + why it crosses + index of
   kept proposals).
6. Write `experiments/report.md` (see below).

**Final roll-up — `experiments/report.md`** (write LAST, after the critique+filter
pass). Must contain:
- **Filter counts.** Candidates drafted vs kept vs filtered, overall and per
  category: e.g. "drafted 48 across 6 categories → kept 31, filtered 17; 1 whole
  category dropped." A small table (category | drafted | kept | filtered) + totals.
- **Worked filter examples — show the judgment, not just numbers:**
  - 2-3 **proposals you FILTERED OUT**, each with a one-paragraph reason (what the
    `## Critique` found: too small, already implicit, risky, no precedent).
  - 2-3 **agendas/categories you FILTERED OUT** (if any), with the reason none of
    their proposals survived.
  - 2-3 **proposals you KEPT as-is**, spread across 2-3 different agendas, each with
    one line on why it survived (strong precedent, large runtime fraction, clean
    localization).
- Keep it skimmable — this is the executive summary of the discovery run.

**Quality bar / edge cases**
- Every cited file/function/line MUST exist in the on-disk source (verify, don't
  guess). A localization that points at a stale or imagined path is a reject.
- "New" is strict: incremental configs of an existing kernel are not novel; a
  genuinely un-fused op pair, an fp16 tensor with no fp8 path, a CUDA kernel with
  no ROCm/TPU twin, a recompute with no cache — those are novel.
- Prefer proposals where the agenda's own evidence shows the pattern already paid
  off elsewhere (reuse the proven lever on an unproven site) — those carry the
  best expected-gain argument.
- State uncertainty honestly; a well-localized "medium-confidence" proposal beats a
  confident hand-wave.
